 "title": "Home / Newton County, Indiana",
 "text": "Home / Newton County, Indiana\nSkip over navigation\nNewton County\nThe Official Government Website for Newton County, Indiana\nDocuments | Site Tools\nSearch\nSearch Submit\nStart Content\nWillow Slough Fish & Wildlife Area - Courtesy of Firkins Films\nGeorge Ade Home - Courtesy of Firkins Films\nGovernment Center Log Cabin - Courtesy of Firkins Films\nKankakee Sands Bison Herd - Courtesy of Firkins Films\nprev next\nToggle Menu\nHome\nAbout Community Events\nCounty Demographics\nDocument Center\nEmployment Opportunities\nEvents Calendar\nResident Information\nCourthouse Assessor\nAuditor\nClerk\nCourts\nProbation\nProsecutor\nRecorder\nTreasurer\nCourthouse Directory\nGovernment Center Adult Education\nBuilding Department\nCoroner's Office\nCounty Commissioners Commissioners Meeting Schedule\nMeet Your Commissioners\nCounty Council Council Meeting Schedule\nMeet Your Council Members\nHealth Department\nPark Board\nPurdue Extension\nRecycling\nSoil & Water Conservation District\nVeteran's Service Officer\nWIC\nWorkOne\nCounty Facilities Ambulance Service\nAnimal Control\nCommunications Center\nDepartment Child Services\nDivision of Family Resources\nEmergency Management Agency\nHighway Department\nMaintenace Department\nMap of County Offices\nSearch Locations by Name\nSurveyor's Office\nSheriff Dept In Remembrance\nNewton County Jail\nContact Ask a Question\nBoards & Commissions Board of Zoning Appeals\nDrainage Board\nPlan Commission\nPlat Commission\nCounty Departments A-G Ambulance Services\nAnimal Control\nAssessor's Office\nAuditor's Office\nBuilding Department\nClerk of Courts\nCoroner's Office\nEconomic Development\nElections & Voting\nEmergency Management Agency\nEmergency Medical Services\nGIS Services\nCounty Departments H-Z Health Department\nHighway Department\nMaintenance Department\nNewton County Extension Office\nProbation Department\nProsecutor's Office\nRecorder's Office\nRecycling\nSheriff's Department\nSoil & Water Conservation District\nSurveyor's Office\nTreasurer's Office\nZoning\nVeteran's Service Officer\nSubmit an Online Form\nView the County Staff Directory\nEmployee Resources Doculivery\nEmployee Webmail\nEmployment Application\nWelcome to Newton County\nThe original Newton County was formed by statute on February 7, 1835, and was a roughly square area some 30 miles on a side, encompassing what is now the northern half of the county, the northern half of Jasper County, and a large section to the north. The northern border was cut back to the Kankakee River on February 1, 1836, with all land north of the Kankakee River going to Lake and Porter counties. The county was abolished and combined with Jasper County in 1839. On December 8, 1859, the county was re-created and the borders were redrawn to essentially their current state. Read more...\nBreaking News\nMore Like This\nJob Posting: Newton County Economic Development Administrative Support Services\nNewton County Multi Hazard Mitigation plan\nNewton County Tax Sale is September 28, 2026 in the Commissioner's Room at the Courthouse at 9 am CST\nCommunity\nCalendar\nGIS\nData\nResource\nGuide\nOnline\nPayments\nEconomic\nDevelopment\nElection\nInformation\nBlackboard\nConnect\nContact Us\n201 N 3rd St\nKentland, IN 47951\nGet Directions\nPhone: (888) 663-9866\nOffice Hours:\nMonday-Friday: 8:00 am - 4:00 pm\nSite Design and Content Copyright © 2026 Newton County, IN\nSite Design and Content Management by\nCORE Business Technologies\nPrivacy Policy\nAccessibility Statement\nTerms of Use",
